WEBVTT

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.000
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:09.500
"Episode 10: Decision"

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.200
"391: Anonymous YOLO.
Maybe they'll appear if we attack Yoshiaki?"
"392: Anonymous YOLO. I just went
and ransacked Yoshiaki's place. LOLOL"

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:17.000
"394: Anonymous YOLO. I think I found
a different video that looks like them."
"395: Anonymous YOLO. Where? Post the link."

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:21.500
The scariest thing in the world is the public...

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:31.580
"Complete Denial of All Charges"

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.040
There's no work for you here.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.120
What are we going to do now?

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.870
Looks like this will be our home for a while.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.620
I guess this is what we deserve.

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:06.450
I was thinking of telling
the two of them the truth.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.160
I was thinking the same thing.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:19.500
Eat. You might not have an appetite, but...

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:22.160
Geek is currently looking at my bike.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:27.410
It'll take some time to get fixed,
so you should rest until then...

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.540
Takuya.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.410
I'm sorry.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:35.910
You should thank me here, not apologize.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.200
I can't believe you made it out safely.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.330
Did you know that'd happen, Yumiko?

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:57.660
No way. I'm just as surprised as you are.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:07.330
At the time, I thought to myself,
"Oh, I'm going to die."

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.950
My vision got dark, but then...

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:21.370
Impossible!

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:26.160
There's no way he'd save you or Yumiko
after you went against the Agency!

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:29.790
You're the one misunderstanding Mr. Kaibara.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:33.660
Then why did he stop my
undercover investigation?

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:35.750
If we had exposed the
evildoings of the academy,

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.500
we could have saved the children!

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.660
Because he sided with the Agency...

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:45.290
I understand how you feel, sir.

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:48.290
But I looked into it afterwards.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:49.290
Kouta.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:51.620
Please let me tell him.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:58.250
We had no choice at the time.
Mr. Kaibara saved you!

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.950
Mr. Kaibara was threatened by the Agency.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.870
If he didn't obey, they were going to kill
everyone in the detective agency.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:15.450
He went against his values
in order to save our lives.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:19.660
He's the most frustrated
one out of all of us.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.750
Shit...

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.330
Here. This has underwear
and various necessities.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.450
Takuya can't really help you
with these kinds of things.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.120
Thank you.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.120
Yuki. Listen.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:50.000
I know it's cruel to tell you this now,
but the Lost is not over.

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:53.660
What do you mean?

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.500
The Lost is expanding as we speak.

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:05.790
Considering the energy used to trigger the Lost,
it should have expanded to about this size.

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.120
This much?!

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:14.250
So, in other words, it isn't finished yet
and is slowly growing to completion.

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:18.370
Of course, this is a problem that
the entire world will have to face.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:23.910
The earliest it will be is decades from now.
There isn't an imminent danger.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:29.870
If that hole had properly connected, the Noah
Project would have been complete.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:34.000
Is this really Daichi's doing?

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.540
It must be. He is using some
method to stop the expansion.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.000
But, I cannot imagine that
he's still alive in there...

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:48.540
We have tried to send messages
into Lost many times, however...

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.450
But there was one time that a
message was received from Lost.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.450
Are you saying that was from Daichi?

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.040
Yes.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:01.660
Yuki must be heading toward Lost
because of some message she received.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:04.080
Let Yuki run free and have her awaken.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.790
Or have Souma go berserk.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:11.370
I believed either would be enough
to substitute for the portal device.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.450
But it was simpler than I thought.

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:19.080
As long as we eliminate Daichi,
the portal will reach completion.

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:22.540
Yuki?

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:25.830
You said it will take decades,

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:29.500
but the hole will eventually
swallow everything, right?

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:34.120
I have to go and do something about it.
Father is calling for me.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.290
Even that message may be
a trap set by the enemy!

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.040
Are you telling me to stop because of that?

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:43.910
If there is even the
slightest chance, I will go.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:50.660
Then, let me tell you the true danger of Lost...

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:52.370
Dissolve the contract?

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:53.200
Yeah.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:58.950
After everything that happened?
Weren't we delivering Yuki to Lost?

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:02.500
There is something I haven't told you.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:06.620
Eliminate Daichi? How?

00:08:06.620 --> 00:08:09.500
I will head to Lost myself.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:15.160
Are you serious?! You know how
dangerous the surge particles are!

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:20.950
All of our experiments until now were in order
to become unaffected by such a thing.

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:25.870
The medicine is incomplete.
If a normal human stepped into Lost...

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.160
What are surge particles?

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:34.500
An unknown type of particle that
permeates through all of Lost.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.450
It has devastating effects on the
nervous systems of living creatures.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.250
If you are exposed to it for long periods,

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:44.250
it erodes the hippocampus
and causes memory loss.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:50.120
At worst, it causes abnormalities in
your mental state and you may die.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:56.120
I am sure that's why there have been no
survivors from any of the survey teams.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.330
So?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:03.750
You sent Yuki and me to Lost
even though you knew that, right?

00:09:03.750 --> 00:09:09.620
Yeah. But we can't put the two
of you in any more danger.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:13.500
You may think I'm being selfish,
but this is how I truly feel.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:17.120
The director of Lacuna Chemical, Taiyo,
has started to move.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.620
Taiyo?!

00:09:18.620 --> 00:09:20.870
That guy, huh?

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.410
It seems he is trying to communicate
with something in Lost.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:29.370
If Yuki moves, he will come to eliminate her.
He is a dangerous man.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:34.200
So, Yuki, please. Don't go.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:48.250
Here! Look!

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:51.200
Yua-<i>tan</i>'s movements just now! Did you see?!

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:51.750
No?

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:54.290
Jeez. Look carefully!

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.910
Here! She fell one tempo behind.

00:09:56.910 --> 00:10:00.700
But Yua-<i>tan </i>made it through with ad-libbing!

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:01.500
I see...

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:07.370
Isn't that amazing? Everyone calls her devious,
but she works harder than anyone else.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:10.040
Yua-<i>tan </i>really pays attention
to her surroundings!

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.330
I see.

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:15.660
Oh, if you're hungry, help yourself to some
<i>tenmusu </i>rice balls and potato chips!

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:18.410
You always eat these two together.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.700
I'm telling you, they taste the best together!

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.500
Here! Try it, Takuya.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:25.830
Okay. Now comes the<i> tenmusu</i>!

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.660
Is that what you mean by together?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:29.160
Just do it!

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:32.120
See! There it is! Isn't your
mouth in heaven right now?

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.750
The collaboration of crunchy and juicy!

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:41.580
Oh, it's Yua-<i>tan</i>'s solo song!
The lyrics here are the best!

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.700
T-Takuya!

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:55.830
Wait a second!

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:02.450
"Supreme Five
~Beyond Our Dream~"
I'll lend this to you!

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.410
I watched this with you already.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:07.160
It's the best, no matter
how many times you see it!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:12.040
You better return it. It's my treasure.

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.160
Yeah.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:26.000
This is a great view.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.540
Yeah.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.700
Yuki.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:46.500
What's the first thing you want to do
once your life returns to normal?

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:47.700
Huh?

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.080
Well...

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:55.040
Normal life, huh? I didn't even think about it.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.410
Too many things have happened.

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:05.750
The scooter hasn't been doing too well.
Will you give me a little more time?

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:08.790
Oh, yeah... I understand.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:14.620
What did you say?!

00:12:14.620 --> 00:12:17.500
So Takuya was an experiment
for you from the beginning?!

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:19.040
Calm down!

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:22.450
If that's the case, you guys are
no different from the Agency!

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.870
True.

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:28.000
Pushing them forward. Holding them back.
You really do whatever you want.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.410
Miss Yumiko...

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:33.830
Stopping them like that would only
make it more painful for those two.

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:54.160
As I thought, this line is the limit.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:05.620
The balance of ingredients in the
surge-particle-blocking drug

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.790
should be correct in theory.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:12.120
But there must be some
essential factor we are missing.

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.250
Prepare more test subjects.

00:13:14.250 --> 00:13:16.120
But, any more than this...

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:20.330
As long as the portal connects,
the Agency will no longer matter.

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:21.330
Hurry.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:22.500
Yes.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:35.450
Now, didn't they talk about
cabbage last night on TV?

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.910
That it was good for the skin?

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.540
Oh, but you don't really
need something like that!

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.700
Oh, my! I guess I'll take one!

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:43.250
Thanks for the business!

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.620
How did you do on the test?

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:46.080
I did real bad in English.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:49.160
Me, too. I did pretty bad in world history,
math, and Japanese, too.

00:13:49.160 --> 00:13:50.790
That's terrible!

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:53.450
No fair, Sis!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:55.290
I want to learn piano, too!

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:57.580
You don't have the ear for it, so you can't.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.660
You're ugly, so you can't.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:02.830
Mom! He's been so bratty lately!

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:04.450
Huh?

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:10.120
Wait. Why me? Go tell him yourself!

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:11.540
Huh? Why tomatoes?

00:14:11.540 --> 00:14:13.290
Shh!

00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:15.250
Hello, Miss Yumiko?

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:18.870
Jeez, this is so troublesome...

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:23.290
What is it?

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:26.330
Sir? You're free now aren't you?
You're free, right?!

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.500
Will you go buy some tomatoes?

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.450
Huh?

00:14:29.450 --> 00:14:33.450
Well, Miss Yumiko wants
to make some pescatora.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.910
She says she wants to focus
on the right ingredients.

00:14:35.910 --> 00:14:38.370
Um, what tomato did she say again?

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:42.660
Anyways, she says she has to
have that certain type of tomato.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:47.160
I've never seen her cook before.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:51.000
I'll text you the place. Please take care of it!

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:52.500
Hey!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:58.290
What the hell...?

00:15:00.660 --> 00:15:05.040
Lately, I often think back to
when we were at the lab.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:10.580
At the time, we were proud of being
at the forefront of research.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:12.160
It was fulfilling.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:17.370
For me, too. A scientist couldn't
ask for a better environment.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:21.200
After all, we had a genius
like Mr. Daichi with us.

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:25.200
He was a strange man,
but he loved his family very much.

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:28.580
Every time he opened his mouth,
it was about Yuki and Souma.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.620
They call that a doting parent.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.700
Just...

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.830
I wonder what Mr. Daichi truly
thought about his research.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:45.330
Eiji. Science can become poison or
medicine depending on how it is used.

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:49.580
We are also partially responsible for the Lost.

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:53.080
We have to face that responsibility.

00:15:53.080 --> 00:15:56.370
Saying the words is easy.
Do you have the conviction?

00:15:56.370 --> 00:16:01.950
Yeah. I want to put being a
human before being a scientist.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:08.040
No matter what happens,
we will fully support their decision.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.450
You haven't had something
like this in a while, right?

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.870
An occasional break is important.

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:46.830
Hey, want to eat some tomatoes?

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:53.120
Is that enough water?

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:54.790
You'd think so, right?

00:16:54.790 --> 00:17:00.500
At first, I watered them a lot.
But the tomatoes didn't taste that great.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:05.160
I think I ended up stealing
the plants' will to live.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:08.410
This is the right amount to grow them hardy.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:10.950
Here.

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:12.750
They're delicious.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:20.830
As I thought. Takuya knew
about the surge particles.

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.580
Yes.

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.660
I thought so.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:29.830
You've already decided, haven't you?

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:34.290
Let's get another parfait.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:35.160
Huh?

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:36.870
Let's split one.

00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.830
Yeah.

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:46.700
With that many, Yumiko'll be able to make it
no matter how many times she messes up.

00:17:46.700 --> 00:17:48.330
Thank you.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.450
Takuya.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:56.450
It's your life. Live it how you want.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.450
Let's stop, Taiyo.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:21.290
We are sure of the balance of
ingredients for the inhibitor drug.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:24.000
A missing factor...

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.200
A factor from a parallel universe, not here...

00:18:27.200 --> 00:18:29.450
Since we were originally from there,

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:32.870
isn't it possible for us to enter
while retaining our memory?

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:34.250
We don't have enough evidence for that--

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:38.660
Isn't Daichi's ability to retain his
memory inside of Lost the proof?

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.620
If only we could confirm this hypothesis...

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:47.200
I will... I will be the test subject.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.330
Are you sure?

00:18:53.120 --> 00:18:58.750
It's fine. I won't forget you.

00:18:58.750 --> 00:19:00.410
Tsuki...

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:04.830
Go ahead.

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:23.910
Hoh...

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:27.330
Taiyo?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:31.330
See! I remember you properly!

00:19:31.330 --> 00:19:37.410
Wonderful results. Tsuki, just in case,
let us test the upper limits.

00:19:37.410 --> 00:19:41.410
Huh...? Why?!

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:48.700
Let me out! Hey! Why?! Hey!

00:19:53.660 --> 00:19:56.580
The hypothesis has been confirmed...

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.120
How is the bike?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:06.580
Yeah, it's all fixed up.

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:07.790
I see.

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:13.580
Hey.

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.750
Hm?

00:20:14.750 --> 00:20:18.330
What is normal life to you, Takuya?

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:24.330
Having a place to stay, a place to work,
and some friends to be with.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.410
How normal.

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:29.290
Normal is the best kind of happiness.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:32.580
I see. You're right.

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:35.950
Once everything is over,
I want to live a normal life.

00:20:38.200 --> 00:20:41.000
I wonder what place would be
the best place to live?

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.450
A place with a good view.

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:47.250
A house where you can see the sea.
I'd like a cat, too.

00:20:47.250 --> 00:20:50.870
A big window would be good.
The cat would be happy, too.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:53.410
I wonder what color the curtains should be.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:54.370
Blue.

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:58.290
What? A blue sea behind blue curtains?

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.290
Oh, you're right. Then, green.

00:21:01.290 --> 00:21:04.160
That would be nice.
The furniture should match well, too.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:07.000
I've always dreamed of living
in a fashionable house.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.500
I'll come visit sometimes.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.580
I'll make you something to eat.

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:14.000
Just some coffee and bread are enough.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.040
What are you saying? It has to
be white rice and miso soup!

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.620
The traditional Japanese food-type.

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:23.700
It must be wonderful. A normal life.

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.290
Yeah.

00:21:25.290 --> 00:21:27.410
I have to try my best not to forget.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.450
Yeah. No matter what happens.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:34.330
Let's not forget about living a happy life.

00:21:39.120 --> 00:21:40.580
It's delicious.

